From: FineWine
Subject: [PATCH] nvngx: NGX for Direct3D 12 and Vulkan, with frame generation.

DXMT's nvngx.dll implements NGX for Direct3D 11 only, and only DLSS super resolution. In
FineWine's runtime Direct3D 12 is Wine's vkd3d and Vulkan is Wine's Vulkan layer, both on
MoltenVK, and programs on those paths found no DLSS at all.

nvngx_moltenvk.cpp adds the NVSDK_NGX_D3D12_* and NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_* entry points. An
evaluation becomes a request that FineWine's MoltenVK records in the program's command buffer
as MetalFX work: super resolution (feature 1) as a temporal upscale, frame generation
(feature 11, the DLSSG.* parameters) as a frame interpolation. A Vulkan program's request goes
out through vkCmdPushConstants(); a Direct3D 12 program's goes through two private data GUIDs
of FineWine's vkd3d.

The module now also loads when FINEWINE_DLSS=1 is set, not only when DXMT's DXGI has its
NVIDIA extension on: a Direct3D 12 or Vulkan program may not be using DXMT's DXGI.

diff --git a/src/nvngx/meson.build b/src/nvngx/meson.build
index b94ad4b..0dc9a20 100644
